mpp_buf_slot ships an alignment self-check that computes the frame buffer size
twice (legacy vs sys_cfg) and logs "mismatch size_total A - B" whenever the two
formulas disagree. This is purely diagnostic: MPP actually uses the sys_cfg
result (use_legacy_align defaults to 0), i.e. the larger, HW-correct size, so
nothing is undersized or reallocated. The check is enabled by default because
buf_slot_debug defaults to include BUF_SLOT_DBG_INFO_SET. Drop that bit from the
default mask so the benign per-slot log stops spamming; it can still be turned
back on via `buf_slot_debug=0x800`.

--- a/mpp/base/mpp_buf_slot.c
+++ b/mpp/base/mpp_buf_slot.c
@@ -820,7 +820,7 @@
     }
 
     mpp_env_get_u32("buf_slot_debug", &buf_slot_debug,
-                    BUF_SLOT_DBG_OPS_HISTORY | BUF_SLOT_DBG_INFO_SET);
+                    BUF_SLOT_DBG_OPS_HISTORY);
     mpp_env_get_u32("use_legacy_align", &use_legacy_align, 0);
 
     do {
